          "date": "2026-11-20 18:18:30.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21277 tests: always restart mds1 in sanity-hsm 606",
        "message": "LU-21277 tests: always restart mds1 in sanity-hsm 606\n\ntest_606 stops mds1, remounts its device as ldiskfs or zfs, and\nregisters a single EXIT trap that unmounts that mountpoint and\nstarts mds1 again.  If the umount fails with EBUSY, set -e aborts\nthe trap before \"start mds1\", so MDT0000 stays down.  test_607b\nthen hangs until the test system's 24 hour limit.\n\nSplit the cleanup into three stack_trap commands, which run in\nreverse order of registration: retry the umount for up to 60s,\nthen unmount_fstype to restore the device, then start mds1.  The\n\"|| true\" on the first two keeps a failed umount from skipping the\nrestart, and lets unmount_zfs restore the dataset mountpoint\nproperty even when the retry loop already unmounted it.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=sanity-hsm env=ONLY=\"606 607b\"\nSigned-off-by: John Grasso <johgras@amazon.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I4295966791b52747c293c6c229e31c1aa6e9ff11\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
